  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "The only thing remarkable about the sheets is that the uncommons sheet depicted at the link above has a blank spot in the top left corner.",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "Another variant of the sheet, auctioned recently on Ebay, replaces the gap with an Exeggutor:",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "The choice of which cards appear more frequently on the sheets appears more or less random (non-holo Flareon is more common than non-holo Jolteon and Vaporeon, for example).",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "The commons and uncommons sheets are different to accomodate striped collation without including duplicate cards in booster packs.",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "The rare and holo sheets may be the same as for the other variants, or they may be different.",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "The direction the cards are inserted into the packs varies sometimes within a set, i.e. one box may be left to right, top to bottom and another right to left, bottom to top.",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "Occasionally, cards are out of sequence, the most common “error” being when two cards are flipped in sequence.",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
    "sourceId": 4,
    "key": "rarity-guide",
    "quote": "not all commons in box apparently come from the same sheet, there are usually 2-3 stacks of commons getting inserted into packs alternatingly",
    "evidencePath": "docs/research/phase5/jungle/rarity-guide.text.txt",
    "evidenceSha256": "a05087035401a3fbcd4170883ef649ead9b2f3b04ef9c1d3fda526af94c44d1c",
    "verbatimVerified": true
  },
  {
